   "summary": "Commenters split between those defending the existing childhood vaccine schedule and those wanting more parental choice and a reduced schedule. Supporters of the current system stress that vaccines save lives, that outbreaks like measles are returning, and that extra categories or shared decision-making defaults would add confusion, burden clinics and risk insurance coverage. Others argue for informed consent, bodily autonomy and parental rights, oppose any mandates, and some want more vaccines, such as HPV and varicella, moved to shared decision-making. Many entries are a identical form-letter urging careful consideration without stating a position, and one is just an insult.",
