   "summary": "Nearly all commenters defend California's Coastal Management Program and oppose any move to weaken it, treating the federal evaluation as unnecessary or a pretext for pressure. Many argue the review is redundant because NOAA looked at the program recently, and that it threatens the state's federal consistency authority and federal funding. Others stress the coast's ecological value and its multibillion-dollar economy, and warn of risks from offshore oil, pipelines, and other development. One commenter takes the opposite view, criticizing California's regulation and calling for oil drilling to bring jobs and lower fuel prices. One submission is only an attachment cover note with no stated position.",
