   "summary": "All of the sampled commenters oppose the proposed permitting shortcut for oil and gas production sites in the National Petroleum Reserve in Alaska. Many comments are form-letter text. They argue that each project needs its own full environmental review under NEPA, including cumulative impacts, and that BLM should keep its authority to deny, condition or revoke approvals. They also stress protecting wildlife habitat such as birds, caribou and wetlands, along with subsistence resources and the climate. Several call for keeping public input and Tribal consultation, and criticize the rule as an industry-driven rubber stamp.",
